{"t": 1794115693.9457235, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_add_issue_comment", "args": {"body": "\u26a0\ufe0f This change introduced a production reconciliation bug.\n\nSentry issue: https://acme.sentry.io/issues/LEDGER-WORKER-9A\n\n**LEDGER-WORKER-9A \u2014 ReconciliationMismatch: converted totals off by 1 minor unit** (first seen in release `ledger-worker@2026.11.3`, ~2,201 events).\n\nRoot cause: `worker/rates.py` now truncates with `int(amount_minor * rate)` instead of rounding to the nearest minor unit. When the converted amount lands just below an integer boundary (e.g. 1099.9999999999998), truncation returns 1099 instead of the expected 1100, so reconciled totals are off by one minor unit.\n\nFix: restore rounding in `convert()` (`return round(amount_minor * rate)`).", "issue_number": 412, "owner": "acme", "repo": "ledger-worker"}, "ok": true}
